    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0166" n="154" xml:id="pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12454: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-25T17:00:00+03:00">June 25, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 25—4:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1218. Department’s 840, June 24, 7 p.m. The Soviet Union has not issued a formal
                    proclamation of war against Germany or against Italy. The status of
                    Soviet-German relations was announced in Molotov’s address on June 22,<anchor
                        n="90" xml:id="d160-f1"/> and no reference whatever has been made to
                    Italy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d160-f1" n="90" xml:id="d160-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 1197, June 22, from the Ambassador in the Soviet Union, <ref
                        target="#pg625">p. 625</ref>.</p>
            </note>
